   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear Budgen: If you have time please <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">throw that leaflet</seg> about the <name type="work">Book of the Dead</name> into an envelope. I want it for the artist who is doing the preface to fragment no 4.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>kind regards</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce </name>
                        </signed>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1930-10-08">8.10.930</date>
                        </dateline>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">This was the 43-page booklet, E. A. Wallis Budge’s <name type="work">The Book of the Dead</name> (London: British Museum, 1920, 1922). Vincent Deane details JJ’s notes taken from it in 1930 in <name type="work">The Finnegans Wake Notebooks at Buffalo</name>: Notebook VI.B.32 (Turnhout: Brepols, 2004), 11-14.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
